WEBVTT

00:48.938 --> 00:50.188
Needed their signatures.

00:50.271 --> 00:51.771
I'm telling you, it's not a problem.

00:51.855 --> 00:54.355
We have to wait a little.
The market's gonna turn around

00:54.438 --> 00:56.148
and everything will be fine.

00:58.271 --> 00:59.771
Okay. We have to sell the penthouse.

00:59.855 --> 01:01.355
No. We don't.

01:01.438 --> 01:04.058
-That's, that's--
-What? An actual solution?

01:04.146 --> 01:06.976
Maybe growing up in this place,
you got used to the idea

01:07.063 --> 01:10.113
that a solution will
just fall out of the sky. But it won't.

01:10.188 --> 01:11.648
You've got a daughter to think of.

01:11.730 --> 01:13.310
I've got it under control, Eleanor.

01:18.855 --> 01:20.015
Do you want to?

01:20.521 --> 01:22.111
Who are we kidding? You go.

01:32.188 --> 01:33.188
Kate?

01:36.355 --> 01:37.605
Coming in.

01:39.313 --> 01:40.983
You shouldn't eavesdrop.

01:42.313 --> 01:44.733
Then how would I know
what you're saying when I'm not there?

01:47.230 --> 01:49.400
I don't know how to argue with that.

01:50.271 --> 01:51.771
How much did you hear?

01:52.605 --> 01:54.265
I don't want to move.

01:55.438 --> 01:56.688
That much, huh?

01:59.563 --> 02:01.983
-We don't have to.
-How do you know?

02:02.605 --> 02:05.265
Mommy said things
don't just fall from the sky.

02:05.855 --> 02:08.855
Well, yeah,
but there's always gonna be weather.

02:09.480 --> 02:12.060
Some people forget
the one thing they can control,

02:12.646 --> 02:15.146
the choices they make in the face of it.

02:17.896 --> 02:20.396
What would you do in a hurricane?

02:21.063 --> 02:23.273
I would do what I always do.

02:26.021 --> 02:27.441
Protect you.

02:31.146 --> 02:33.976
Now, why don't you go have
some lunch with your mom?

02:34.063 --> 02:35.153
Think fast.

02:35.855 --> 02:37.305
I'll be downstairs in my office.

02:49.021 --> 02:51.021
Mommies can be
pretty fun, too, you know.

02:51.521 --> 02:53.111
I bet you didn't know I could do this.

03:00.021 --> 03:01.731
Made you smile.

03:03.021 --> 03:04.021
Come on.

03:04.771 --> 03:07.191
Why don't you go grab the <i>Checkers?</i>
We can liven things up.

03:07.771 --> 03:09.401
-All right. Yeah.
-Yeah?

03:09.480 --> 03:11.310
Okay, I'm going downstairs,
I'll be right back.

03:11.396 --> 03:12.396
Okay.

03:34.646 --> 03:36.266
Mommy!

03:36.355 --> 03:38.685
Mommy? Mommy, what's happening?

03:41.355 --> 03:42.645
Mommy!

03:42.730 --> 03:44.520
Daddy, where are you?

03:55.188 --> 03:56.268
Dad?

04:03.980 --> 04:05.730
Dad. Daddy, where are you?

04:10.271 --> 04:11.481
Mommy!

05:29.230 --> 05:30.230
Kate!

05:31.063 --> 05:32.903
We have to get out of here.

05:36.355 --> 05:39.185
Is Daddy okay?

05:40.146 --> 05:41.146
Dad!

05:43.813 --> 05:45.403
Dad! Dad!

05:45.480 --> 05:46.690
<i>Daddy!</i>

05:53.605 --> 05:54.975
I'm so sorry, my dear.

06:02.771 --> 06:04.401
What if they come back?

06:07.188 --> 06:08.648
They won't come back.

06:11.896 --> 06:13.106
How do you know?

06:17.480 --> 06:19.940
Because the heroes
showed them what would happen.

06:20.855 --> 06:23.015
And even though this is scary,

06:24.230 --> 06:26.860
I'm still the luckiest woman in the world

06:26.938 --> 06:29.808
because I have
the greatest little girl in the world.

06:34.230 --> 06:36.150
Who is not that little.

06:39.480 --> 06:42.150
I need to protect us.

06:42.230 --> 06:43.810
Kate, that's my job.

06:45.896 --> 06:46.936
Okay?

06:47.021 --> 06:50.191
Whatever you need, I'm here for you.

06:57.313 --> 06:58.773
I need a bow and arrow.

08:47.896 --> 08:48.896
Ugh! Come on!

09:23.855 --> 09:25.475
<i>Kate, be careful.</i>

09:25.563 --> 09:28.943
<i>If we get caught, you're definitely</i>
<i>gonna be kicked off the archery team.</i>

09:29.021 --> 09:31.611
Yeah, I know. But a bet's a bet, Greer.

09:32.355 --> 09:35.475
Okay, so the real question.

09:35.563 --> 09:39.653
Does the bell swing back and forth,
or the dangly thingy swing back and forth?

09:39.730 --> 09:41.860
It's obviously the bell.

09:41.938 --> 09:44.558
See? I would disagree.

09:44.646 --> 09:46.016
I think it's the dangly thingy.

09:46.105 --> 09:47.895
<i>Nice outfit by the way, Kate.</i>

09:47.980 --> 09:49.270
Yeah, well,

09:50.188 --> 09:52.058
sometimes, you gotta dress the part.

09:52.146 --> 09:53.266
<i>I know it's a bet,</i>

09:53.355 --> 09:55.435
but are you sure
that arrow won't damage it?

09:56.896 --> 09:57.896
No.

10:10.313 --> 10:12.483
Well, that was a bit of a letdown.

10:13.021 --> 10:15.191
Okay, you know what, just hang on.

10:15.730 --> 10:16.940
Hang on.

10:17.480 --> 10:19.770
Let me just fix this. Give me a second.

10:55.938 --> 10:59.518
Oh, my God!
That was amazing! Wow!

10:59.605 --> 11:00.685
Nice, Kate.

11:05.646 --> 11:07.436
That's fine.

11:10.021 --> 11:13.981
Right? I mean, it gives it character.
All famous bells have cracks in them.

11:16.688 --> 11:18.688
All right, that's, uh, that's not great.

11:18.771 --> 11:20.561
<i>But it could be worse.</i>

11:26.355 --> 11:27.515
This is bad.

11:29.563 --> 11:30.563
Hold it!

13:23.521 --> 13:24.771
Dad?

13:26.438 --> 13:27.438
Dad?

13:32.271 --> 13:34.061
Did you turn your hearing aid off?

13:35.563 --> 13:38.523
No, honey, I know what happens.

13:38.605 --> 13:39.805
I was there.

13:39.896 --> 13:42.146
You know who wasn't there?
Is that guy.

13:42.688 --> 13:43.688
Ant-Man.

13:51.146 --> 13:52.646
You look pretty cool though.

13:53.480 --> 13:54.560
That's a plus.

14:25.021 --> 14:26.191
I'll be right back.

14:55.563 --> 14:56.943
-Hmm.

15:04.646 --> 15:07.516
Oh, uh, a selfie
would be really rad, dude.

15:08.063 --> 15:11.023
My kids would flip.
I mean, you're their absolute favorite.

15:11.646 --> 15:12.896
Yeah, uh...

15:14.021 --> 15:15.941
Now's not really the appropriate time.

15:24.313 --> 15:25.613
Is now a better time?

15:38.146 --> 15:39.266
Wow.

15:45.313 --> 15:47.943
-Hey, are you okay?
-Oh, hey, yeah.

15:48.521 --> 15:51.111
Yeah, yeah. I, uh, just wanted
to come out for some, uh...

15:51.938 --> 15:53.188
Some fresh air, is all.

15:53.271 --> 15:56.941
You know it's fine if you don't
wanna watch the show. I mean...

15:58.105 --> 15:59.805
I know everyone misses her, but...

16:00.813 --> 16:02.563
she was your best friend. It's...

16:04.896 --> 16:06.106
Come here, baby.

16:12.313 --> 16:14.983
This whole thing
is a bit ridiculous, isn't it?

16:15.063 --> 16:16.653
A lot ridiculous.

16:16.730 --> 16:18.860
-The Hulk part was great.
-Yeah, I liked the Hulk.

16:18.938 --> 16:20.228
Hey, Dad. Hey, Lila.

16:20.313 --> 16:22.983
Hey, guys! What's up?
What are you doing here?

16:23.063 --> 16:25.983
Why is everyone singing
and dancing about everything?

16:26.063 --> 16:27.983
I don't know.

16:29.855 --> 16:33.105
But it's Christmas in New York.
And we're out of here. Right?

16:33.188 --> 16:34.558
-Yeah.
-Let's go.

16:34.646 --> 16:36.856
-NATHANIEL: All right.
-Let's show Mom what she's missing.

16:36.938 --> 16:38.978
-NATHANIEL: Yeah.
-Come on, bud.

16:46.355 --> 16:47.355
Hey, Mom!

16:47.438 --> 16:49.228
<i>Hey, honey! I missed you.</i>

16:49.313 --> 16:52.063
<i>-Uh, are you in the city?</i>
-KATE: Yeah, I, uh, I am.

16:52.146 --> 16:54.396
I was gonna stop by my place
and then come see you.

16:54.480 --> 16:57.360
<i>Will you come here first, please?</i>
<i>Jack's over.</i>

16:57.438 --> 16:59.148
<i>I want to talk to you about something.</i>

16:59.230 --> 17:01.400
Okay, uh, okay.
I'll, uh, see you soon, Mom.

17:24.396 --> 17:25.646
Good evening, Miss Bishop.

17:25.730 --> 17:28.310
How's it going? Good?
Wife, kids, all good?

17:28.438 --> 17:30.438
Wonderful, wonderful, Merry Christmas!

17:40.938 --> 17:42.648
-ELEANOR: Hi, sweetie.
-KATE: Hi, Mom.

17:45.480 --> 17:46.860
There you are.

17:47.605 --> 17:50.105
Oh, you look amazing.

17:51.521 --> 17:53.191
What are we looking all fancy for?

17:53.271 --> 17:54.691
Charity auction.

17:54.771 --> 17:56.311
-Ugh.
-I know, right?

17:56.396 --> 17:59.646
All those poor people and nonprofits
relying on the more fortunate.

17:59.730 --> 18:01.060
That is not what I meant.

18:01.146 --> 18:04.146
As much as I love having
you home for the holidays,

18:04.230 --> 18:08.190
I'm not thrilled that I'm about
to replace an irreplaceable clock tower.

18:08.271 --> 18:09.981
It was a bell tower.

18:10.063 --> 18:12.613
The Dean said it had a bell and a clock,

18:12.688 --> 18:15.898
and overachiever that you are,
you managed to destroy both.

18:18.480 --> 18:20.610
What can I do to make it better, Mom?

18:21.438 --> 18:23.768
I started by cancelling your credit cards,

18:23.855 --> 18:27.305
and we're going to have a much longer talk
about this tower that you destroyed,

18:27.396 --> 18:28.396
without joking.

18:28.480 --> 18:30.940
I know young people
think they're invincible,

18:31.021 --> 18:34.191
and rich people think they're invincible
and you've always been both.

18:34.313 --> 18:36.863
So take it from someone
who hasn't, you're not.

18:37.438 --> 18:38.808
You will get hurt.

18:38.896 --> 18:41.106
So please, don't go out looking for it.

18:45.480 --> 18:46.650
Sorry, Mom.

18:48.146 --> 18:49.146
Sorry.

18:50.521 --> 18:51.861
Okay.

18:52.396 --> 18:54.436
You get that from your father, you know.

18:54.980 --> 18:57.520
Why don't you start making it up to me

18:57.605 --> 19:01.185
by putting on that red dress in
your bedroom and coming with me tonight?

19:04.230 --> 19:05.770
All right, well, um,

19:07.271 --> 19:08.771
on another note,

19:11.730 --> 19:13.270
I got a new one for the case.

19:14.271 --> 19:16.901
U.S. Open Martial Art Championship.

19:19.605 --> 19:23.975
You're amazing. I still remember
when you got your black belt at 15.

19:24.771 --> 19:28.151
We might have to retire some from
when you were little to make room. Huh?

19:28.230 --> 19:30.480
-I like those.
-ELEANOR: I do, too, hon.

19:30.563 --> 19:31.613
I do, too.

19:35.521 --> 19:37.521
What's with all the swords, Mom?

19:38.938 --> 19:43.188
Hon, uh, there have been a few changes
while you were away this semester.

19:43.730 --> 19:44.730
Ta-da!

19:44.813 --> 19:45.813
Jack?

19:45.896 --> 19:47.556
Oh.

19:47.646 --> 19:49.646
What an unexpected surprise.

19:49.730 --> 19:51.900
All surprises are unexpected.

19:51.980 --> 19:54.060
That can't be right. Is it?

19:54.730 --> 19:56.020
Nice to see you again, Katie.

19:59.730 --> 20:00.980
That was in your mouth.

20:01.063 --> 20:03.313
So it was.

20:04.021 --> 20:07.061
We cannot be late, so go change.

20:07.146 --> 20:10.056
Meet us at the hotel
and we'll talk there. Okay?

20:10.146 --> 20:11.436
-Shall we?
-Let's.

20:11.521 --> 20:12.811
We'll see you at the party.

20:12.896 --> 20:14.396
See you there, honey.

20:14.480 --> 20:15.690
Lots more to talk about.

20:22.771 --> 20:25.021
You look like a maniac.

20:25.105 --> 20:26.605
You're a total crazy person.

20:28.938 --> 20:30.148
Is anybody else hungry?

20:30.230 --> 20:33.060
For some more, like, some more crabs
or maybe get four more crabs?

20:33.146 --> 20:34.976
-What do you think?
-Yes. I could eat three.

20:35.063 --> 20:36.193
-No.
-COOPER: Come on, Dad,

20:36.271 --> 20:38.151
you ordered food for 30 people.

20:38.230 --> 20:40.440
You're going to puke if you have any more.

20:40.521 --> 20:43.691
And if he pukes,
you two are cleaning it up.

20:43.771 --> 20:45.021
I'm not cleaning it up.

20:45.105 --> 20:48.055
Hey, you know what?
You know what's right down the street?

20:48.771 --> 20:52.231
The Christmas tree.
The biggest one you'll see in your life.

20:52.313 --> 20:54.563
It's enormous!
You want to see that after this?

20:54.646 --> 20:56.106
-Yeah!
-Yeah! Let's go.

20:56.188 --> 20:57.728
-Oh, wait, wait, wait.

20:58.396 --> 21:00.766
Momma callin'. Momma's calling. Say "Hi!"

21:00.855 --> 21:02.555
-Hi, Mom!
-Hi, Momma!

21:02.646 --> 21:05.266
Hey, guys! How are ya?

21:05.355 --> 21:06.805
I miss you so much!

21:06.896 --> 21:09.726
-We miss you, too.
-LAURA: <i>How was the show?</i>

21:10.813 --> 21:13.773
It was, uh-- It's over. It was big.

21:13.855 --> 21:15.765
-We left halfway through.
-There you go.

21:15.855 --> 21:16.975
Oh, no!

21:17.521 --> 21:18.861
You guys all good?

21:18.938 --> 21:21.018
<i>Uh, yeah,</i>
<i>it'd be easier if you were here.</i>

21:21.105 --> 21:23.225
I'd be less likely to strangle these kids.

21:23.313 --> 21:25.613
<i>The whole point was for you</i>
<i>to spend time with the kids.</i>

21:25.688 --> 21:28.558
No, I'm kidding.
We're having a really good time.

21:28.646 --> 21:30.436
-We miss you.
-I miss you.

21:30.521 --> 21:32.981
-I can't wait to see you guys tomorrow.
-LILA: <i>Bye, Mom!</i>

21:33.521 --> 21:35.521
-LILA: Bye, Mom! Love you!
-Bye, Mom.

21:35.605 --> 21:37.515
-Talk to you later. See you soon.
-NATHANIEL: Bye-bye.

21:37.605 --> 21:40.475
Well, look, it's six days
until Christmas, okay?

21:40.563 --> 21:43.773
We're gonna do a lot of activities.
What's your favorite one?

21:43.855 --> 21:45.395
-Um, gingerbread house.
-We're doing that!

21:45.480 --> 21:46.560
What do you got?

21:46.646 --> 21:48.766
Uh, Christmas movie marathon.

21:48.855 --> 21:50.105
Movie marathon, awesome!

21:50.188 --> 21:52.648
-Uh, ugly sweaters.
-Ugly Christmas sweaters!

21:52.730 --> 21:55.690
We have to decorate the tree.
There's a thousand things to do.

21:55.771 --> 21:57.981
It's going to be amazing,
but most important thing,

21:58.063 --> 22:00.273
we're going to do it all together.

22:00.355 --> 22:01.895
No. Not holding their hands.

22:01.980 --> 22:03.400
Hold your brothers' hands.

22:04.646 --> 22:05.896
I love you guys.

22:05.980 --> 22:06.980
Love you, too.

22:07.063 --> 22:09.313
It's going to be
the best Barton Christmas ever!

22:09.396 --> 22:10.396
All right?

22:12.521 --> 22:13.611
-Please.
-Yeah.

22:13.688 --> 22:14.808
Dinner is on us.

22:15.438 --> 22:17.768
-Thank you.
-Oh, that's, that's not necessary.

22:17.855 --> 22:20.395
It's necessary. You saved our city.

22:21.021 --> 22:22.981
Oh. Thank you.

22:25.105 --> 22:26.305
Thank you, sir.

22:26.396 --> 22:28.106
-NATHANIEL: Thank you!
-COOPER: Thank you.

22:41.396 --> 22:42.856
Uh, get back to work.

22:52.105 --> 22:54.475
-Excuse me dear, would you--
-Sorry, I'm not a waitress.

22:54.563 --> 22:56.113
You're the little Bishop girl.

22:56.605 --> 22:57.855
Yes, I am.

22:57.938 --> 23:02.108
-Armand. Armand Duquesne.
-Ah.

23:02.188 --> 23:04.858
You used to come to my brownstone
for brunch.

23:04.938 --> 23:06.608
Oh, build your own blintz bar.

23:06.938 --> 23:08.558
Precisely.

23:09.146 --> 23:10.726
You know, it's unfair.

23:10.813 --> 23:15.023
I never looked
that good in a tuxedo in my life.

23:15.105 --> 23:18.475
I'd appreciate it if you wear something
a little more lady-like for the wedding,

23:18.563 --> 23:19.983
so we won't be competing.

23:20.563 --> 23:21.813
What wedding?

23:21.896 --> 23:23.016
You don't know?

23:24.063 --> 23:25.403
Eleanor and Jack.

23:25.521 --> 23:29.771
Oh! Those secretive little love birds!

23:32.771 --> 23:35.691
-WAITER: Can I offer you some champagne?
-Thank you!

23:35.813 --> 23:40.563
Believe me, I've done everything
in my power to talk him out of it.

23:41.105 --> 23:44.765
When he gets something
set in that little mind of his,

23:44.855 --> 23:46.975
he can be quite determined.

23:47.896 --> 23:48.896
Oh.

23:49.646 --> 23:51.396
Seems like he won the jackpot.

23:51.480 --> 23:52.650
You think so?

23:53.313 --> 23:54.813
So does he.

23:54.896 --> 23:56.516
I'm not so sure.

23:59.938 --> 24:01.978
Armand, I wanna go home. I'm bored.

24:02.063 --> 24:05.233
That's no way to talk, Armand.
That's not the way you were brought up.

24:05.313 --> 24:07.153
Come and say hello to Miss Bishop.

24:08.188 --> 24:09.478
Hey.

24:09.563 --> 24:10.563
Hello.

24:11.188 --> 24:12.728
Another Armand, I see.

24:12.813 --> 24:16.653
Yes. I'm Armand the third
and he's Armand the seventh.

24:16.730 --> 24:18.690
I believe that's quite sufficient.

24:18.771 --> 24:23.771
Well, uh, I'm gonna
make my excuses because it seems that

24:23.855 --> 24:26.895
you need to have a chat

24:27.980 --> 24:30.310
with your prize of a mother.

24:31.771 --> 24:34.271
Come on, Armand. Come on, boy!

24:52.771 --> 24:53.771
You're engaged?

24:53.855 --> 24:56.555
Oh, well, I guess
the beans are out of the bag.

24:58.938 --> 25:01.148
Well, can we have a little moment?

25:01.271 --> 25:04.191
Oh, of course, it's almost time
for my other engagement anyway.

25:04.271 --> 25:05.271
Bye.

25:10.230 --> 25:14.190
Babe, I'm sorry,
I'm sorry you found out this way.

25:14.271 --> 25:16.521
I don't know, Mom, this is just like...

25:17.063 --> 25:19.363
-Fast.
-Yeah, yeah, it's fast, yes.

25:19.438 --> 25:22.648
But, you know, it's kind of nice
being swept up in the romance of it.

25:23.521 --> 25:26.231
Is there a part of you
that could be happy for me?

25:28.855 --> 25:30.145
Yes.

25:30.230 --> 25:31.690
Yes, Mom, of course.

25:33.230 --> 25:36.440
I'm sorry. I'm sorry,
I wanted to tell you first. I'm sorry.

25:37.271 --> 25:39.521
-I'm going to get some air, Mom.
-I understand.

25:39.605 --> 25:40.765
Yep.

25:40.855 --> 25:43.225
-Come back and find me, okay?
-KATE: Yeah.

26:04.896 --> 26:07.016
-Hi.

26:08.396 --> 26:10.056
Heck of a party, huh?

26:27.521 --> 26:30.401
I should've known
that this empire of yours

26:30.480 --> 26:32.190
would be built on a lie.

26:32.313 --> 26:35.903
By myself from the ground up.
So whatever you think you saw is not true.

26:35.980 --> 26:37.610
Don't insult my intelligence.

26:37.730 --> 26:39.440
You're frankly insulting us both.

26:39.521 --> 26:41.521
-I know what I saw.
-You are all just--

26:41.605 --> 26:44.015
Don't you try that on me.

26:46.063 --> 26:48.693
I gave you an opportunity
to explain yourself.

26:48.771 --> 26:50.401
I don't want to argue with you.

26:50.480 --> 26:55.310
I've got powerful friends, too.
The kind you don't want to mess with.

26:56.105 --> 26:57.105
Please.

26:57.313 --> 26:58.313
Armand!

27:03.771 --> 27:05.651
See you at Christmas dinner.

27:08.438 --> 27:10.518
Mom, what was that about?
Is that guy threatening you?

27:10.605 --> 27:13.515
I honestly-- I have no idea.

27:13.938 --> 27:15.438
Why are you lurking in the hallways?

27:15.521 --> 27:18.021
-KATE: I was outside getting air.
-Come back to the party.

27:18.105 --> 27:19.515
-KATE: Okay. All right.
-Okay.

27:19.980 --> 27:21.860
-KATE: Be right there.
-ELEANOR: All right.

27:41.146 --> 27:42.606
-Be right back.
-Okay.

27:56.771 --> 27:58.771
Gary wants you to bring
these down, right away.

27:58.855 --> 28:00.265
-Just these two?
-These two.

28:47.688 --> 28:48.898
This seat is taken.

28:53.938 --> 28:57.438
Ladies and gentlemen,
please be seated, and we will begin.

28:57.521 --> 29:00.231
I've reached
my breaking point with your fiancée.

29:01.313 --> 29:04.153
Things are about to get very ugly.

29:04.230 --> 29:06.730
Why don't we leave Eleanor alone,
you old goat.

29:07.980 --> 29:10.110
For our first item
of the evening,

29:10.188 --> 29:12.938
we will be traveling back in time.

29:13.021 --> 29:17.401
We'll start the bidding for this
magnificent skull at $2 million.

29:17.480 --> 29:18.650
Do I hear $2 million?

29:18.730 --> 29:20.690
<i>Bidder bidder,</i> two-point-one.

29:20.771 --> 29:22.691
I got $2 million,
do I hear two-point-one?

29:22.771 --> 29:25.561
Two-point-one, thank you so much, sir.
Do I hear two-point-two?

29:25.646 --> 29:27.556
-Do I hear two-point-two?
-Excuse me?

29:28.230 --> 29:29.360
Hey, excuse me!

29:31.480 --> 29:32.560
Oh, perfect!

29:34.105 --> 29:35.265
-Oh.
-Great.

29:35.813 --> 29:37.773
I was supposed
to be the only one working here.

29:38.980 --> 29:42.270
Gary? Gary sent me to work here.

29:43.313 --> 29:45.563
So maybe if you want to bother Gary...

29:47.188 --> 29:49.268
You're doing great. Okay.

29:50.188 --> 29:51.978
Two million seven,
now two million eight.

29:52.105 --> 29:54.225
I've got two million seven
right here, going once.

29:54.896 --> 29:57.266
I've got two-point-seven going twice.

29:58.396 --> 30:01.306
Sold for $2.7 million.

30:01.396 --> 30:06.016
Thank you. And I will remind you
that this is for home display only.

30:06.563 --> 30:09.193
And you have no idea where you got it.

30:14.063 --> 30:15.653
Who told you to come down here?

30:16.688 --> 30:17.728
Gary.

30:18.438 --> 30:19.898
I'm Gary.

30:20.313 --> 30:21.313
What's your name?

30:21.938 --> 30:24.058
You see that's the problem, Gary,

30:25.105 --> 30:26.765
you don't even know my name.

30:27.605 --> 30:30.855
You know, uh, this is,
this is not gonna work out. I quit.

30:30.938 --> 30:33.108
You can't quit. Hold on.

30:38.063 --> 30:39.313
Where did she go?

30:40.021 --> 30:41.401
Excuse me.

31:02.938 --> 31:04.398
Come on, let's go. Move.

31:04.730 --> 31:05.980
Don't forget your positions.

31:07.063 --> 31:08.313
Mine's on the left.

31:08.396 --> 31:09.396
Yeah, bro.

31:10.313 --> 31:11.313
Get ready.

31:13.855 --> 31:16.305
Up next,
we have a very special piece.

31:16.396 --> 31:20.606
An artifact recovered from
the wreckage of the Avengers compound.

31:21.230 --> 31:25.650
Now you may recall the Ronin decimated
the criminal underworld of the city,

31:25.730 --> 31:31.270
almost completely annihilating the status
and power of the head of organized crime.

31:31.355 --> 31:35.185
The Ronin brought
a brutal form of justice to his victims,

31:35.271 --> 31:40.021
and his identity continues
to remain a mystery to this very day.

31:40.563 --> 31:44.773
Now you can own
this one-of-a-kind retractable sword,

31:44.855 --> 31:47.475
and we'll start the bidding at $200,000.

31:47.563 --> 31:49.943
Do I hear $200,000? $200,000,

31:50.021 --> 31:51.861
<i>bidder bidder,</i> do I hear $250,000?

31:51.938 --> 31:54.308
$250,000, thank you, sir.
Do I hear $300,000?

31:54.396 --> 31:56.606
$300,000, looking for $350,000.

31:56.688 --> 31:58.268
What are you doing, you dope?

31:59.230 --> 32:00.860
I'm buying that sword.

32:00.938 --> 32:03.308
You don't have 300 grand.

32:04.605 --> 32:07.395
No, but I'll inherit it one day, won't I?

32:08.938 --> 32:11.148
-$350,000.
-$350,000, right here in the front.

32:11.230 --> 32:14.360
Do we go to $400,000?
Let's go to four. Four, thank you so much.

32:14.438 --> 32:16.728
At $400,000, do I hear $450,000?

32:21.646 --> 32:22.806
Moving to two.

32:22.896 --> 32:24.226
Okay, everybody ready?

32:32.688 --> 32:34.648
$440,000, do I hear $450,000?

32:34.730 --> 32:37.440
$450,000 up front. Looking for $475,000.

32:38.188 --> 32:39.438
Come on, ladies and gentlemen.

32:39.521 --> 32:42.111
This sword belonged to the infamous Ronin.

32:43.271 --> 32:44.651
$475,000.

32:44.730 --> 32:46.940
$475,000, <i>bidder bidder,</i>
do I hear $500,000?

32:47.021 --> 32:49.401
I've got $475,000 here, it's going once.

32:50.688 --> 32:52.608
$475,000 is going twice.

32:54.105 --> 32:57.055
Sold for $475,000.

32:57.146 --> 32:59.806
Up next, we have lot number 3-0-9.

32:59.896 --> 33:03.106
The companion piece, the Ronin suit.

33:53.938 --> 33:55.438
Help! Please help!

33:55.521 --> 33:57.151
Security!

33:57.730 --> 33:59.270
We're stuck in here!

34:01.313 --> 34:03.153
We've got 90 seconds
to find the watch.

34:03.230 --> 34:04.860
Everything else is secondary.

34:04.938 --> 34:05.938
Let's go, bro.

34:06.021 --> 34:08.271
-MAN 3: Spread out. Let's go, let's go.

34:09.813 --> 34:11.153
Find the watch!

34:30.730 --> 34:32.440
Where is it? Where is it?

34:32.521 --> 34:34.361
Come on! We're running out of time!

34:36.063 --> 34:37.193
Come on. Let's go.

34:43.396 --> 34:44.476
Grab my hand!

34:45.230 --> 34:46.940
I can't see.

34:48.563 --> 34:50.193
Do you know who I am?

35:00.813 --> 35:01.813
Hello.

35:06.230 --> 35:08.440
Quick, hurry!
Everyone get out of here!

35:08.521 --> 35:12.611
I see him! I see him, there!

35:23.980 --> 35:25.110
Okay.

35:26.646 --> 35:27.686
Come on, Kate.

35:36.521 --> 35:37.521
He disappeared!

35:38.021 --> 35:39.561
I'm telling you, it was the Ronin!

35:40.896 --> 35:43.056
He's here somewhere, bro!
Keep looking!

35:43.146 --> 35:44.146
Oh, shit!

36:14.146 --> 36:15.306
He's getting away!

36:18.938 --> 36:19.938
Darling!

36:20.646 --> 36:23.106
-Where's Kate? She won't answer the phone.
-I don't know.

36:23.188 --> 36:24.978
-Are you okay?
-Are you okay?

36:25.063 --> 36:26.113
Yeah. I'm fine.

36:44.980 --> 36:46.360
-Ronin?

37:34.521 --> 37:36.941
The watch. I found it.

37:38.771 --> 37:40.231
Hey!

37:41.563 --> 37:42.863
Get off me!

37:42.938 --> 37:44.938
I'm gonna get you, you dumb dog!

37:45.021 --> 37:47.021
-Ow! Aah!

37:47.105 --> 37:48.265
I kill you!

37:49.438 --> 37:50.608
Hey!

37:53.146 --> 37:54.976
-KATE: Wait!

38:00.230 --> 38:02.690
Wait! Wait, wait, wait! Wait!

38:03.271 --> 38:05.691
-Oh, wait! Wait! No, no, no.

38:20.688 --> 38:22.808
Kazi! Kazi!

38:22.896 --> 38:24.686
-We gotta go!
-MAN 2: Let's go, bro!

38:25.313 --> 38:27.483
Kazi! We go now! Come on!

38:28.938 --> 38:30.768
Let's get to the van
and go after her.

38:42.021 --> 38:45.271
You were right about the tree, Dad.
It was amazing.

38:45.355 --> 38:46.805
I want one that big.

38:46.896 --> 38:48.556
It wouldn't fit
in our house, dummy.

38:48.646 --> 38:50.806
Please, please, please?

38:50.896 --> 38:53.476
It's a little late for TV, guys.
I've gotta pack.

38:55.230 --> 38:56.520
Ay, ay, ay.

38:57.188 --> 38:59.268
<i>We are following a breaking news story.</i>

38:59.355 --> 39:02.475
<i>A high society gala rocked by an explosion</i>

39:02.605 --> 39:06.435
<i>when it went off at Park Avenue</i>
<i>and 68th Street tonight.</i>

39:06.521 --> 39:08.981
<i>The cause of the explosion</i>
<i>is still under investigation.</i>

39:09.063 --> 39:13.813
<i>But witnesses captured cell phone footage</i>
<i>of a masked assailant fleeing the scene.</i>

39:15.563 --> 39:16.563
Check it out.

39:17.146 --> 39:18.896
A ninja saved a dog.

39:18.980 --> 39:21.860
<i>Authorities believe</i>
<i>the assailant could be the Ronin...</i>

39:21.938 --> 39:23.438
Isn't that awesome, Dad?

39:23.521 --> 39:26.191
<i>...who terrorized</i>
<i>organized crime in New York and elsewhere.</i>

39:38.480 --> 39:42.480
<i>This is the first</i>
<i>potential sighting of the Ronin in years.</i>

39:46.355 --> 39:47.645
Welcome to my apartment.

39:47.771 --> 39:50.271
Whoa. Okay, that was, that was crazy.

39:50.355 --> 39:53.105
But we're safe. We're safe.

39:53.188 --> 39:55.648
Okay, what is going on with Armand?

39:55.730 --> 39:58.520
Threatening my mom
and buying black market swords?

39:58.605 --> 40:00.975
Do you think he's connected
to the break-in somehow?

40:04.021 --> 40:06.481
-Food. You want food. Uh, of course. Oh.

40:06.563 --> 40:07.653
Uh...

40:08.313 --> 40:10.193
Okay, listen. Just hang on.

40:10.271 --> 40:12.521
I'm gonna... I'm gonna get you some food.

40:12.605 --> 40:13.605
Uh...

40:14.605 --> 40:16.305
Pizza? You want some pizza?

40:16.396 --> 40:17.396
Okay.

40:18.271 --> 40:19.981
Have some. Go on.

40:20.063 --> 40:21.693
Good boy. Wow.

40:22.605 --> 40:23.805
You like pizza.

40:25.438 --> 40:27.978
I've got to figure out
what's up with Armand.

40:31.188 --> 40:32.188
Okay.

40:34.563 --> 40:35.983
Do not destroy this apartment.

41:39.605 --> 41:41.185
Monogrammed butterscotch?

42:16.355 --> 42:17.355
Armand?

42:18.188 --> 42:19.268
Oh, God!

42:22.230 --> 42:23.230
Mr. Duquesne?

42:23.313 --> 42:25.313
I have your dry cleaning,
and I brought dinner.

42:55.063 --> 42:58.363
Where do you think you're going?
We only want to talk.

42:58.438 --> 43:01.188
Hey,
we got little surprise for you.

43:01.271 --> 43:03.191
We've got eyes everywhere.

43:03.896 --> 43:05.396
We missed you, Ronin.

43:08.355 --> 43:09.935
We got you now, bro.

43:10.688 --> 43:12.728
Why you makin' it so tough on us, bro?

44:16.313 --> 44:17.403
Sorry.

44:32.813 --> 44:33.983
Oh, come on.

44:41.813 --> 44:42.943
Come on!

44:43.646 --> 44:45.226
You're... You're Hawkeye!

44:45.938 --> 44:47.688
And who the hell are you?
